                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "SoulCalibur 6 is so far the final instalment of the SoulCalibur series, and if I'm honest it's easy to see why. When this game launched it launched with maybe 1/3 of the character customization options as 5, and with a long, bloated, and oftentimes horrendously unfun single player campaign. Then the DLC started. \"Here, you can have some of the last game's DLC back... pay us again.\" A drip feed of cosmetic DLC into a horrifically shallow customization pool was a good will burner, no matter how good the additional fighters were. \r\n\r\nTurning our heads to the story mode... SoulCalibur has for a long time now dabbled with worthless RPG mechanics, and I think this is the worst its ever been. So many numbers and all of it is trounced by just getting a higher levelled sword. Half-baked as it is, the real problem with Libra of Soul isn't the RPG mechanics or how boring it is... It's the dev time that went into it. Chronicle of Souls was all we really needed for a campaign, and if there needed to be an alternate campaign it should have just been a beefed up version of the main one from Chronicle of Souls! Instead we get Libra, with all its warts, taking up dev time that could have gone to the things players of this series probably care about more- characters and cosmetics. \r\n\r\nLizardman is in this game. You can not play as him. His kit is a half-butchered Sophitia's, with unique weapons and a unique armor set the player can not access for their own create-a-characters. Instead of using dev-time and effort and money to finish Lizardman... they threw those resources into Libra of Soul, a mode no one cares about evidenced by both completion achievements having about a 1%. \r\n\r\nSo if I hate this game so much... why the positive rating? Well... it's SoulCalibur baby. It's still SoulCalibur. It's the only SoulCalibur on Steam. I could talk about not liking Reversal Edges or some other tweaks to the main gameplay but it's honestly all minor. At the end of the day, if you wanna do some bong rips and play some SoulCalibur, SC6 has got you. But don't ever buy this game at full price. It regularly goes for like six bucks during sales (thirty with all the DLC), and I would argue it isn't worth it full price. Here's hoping bamco comes back to SoulCalibur some day... and here's hoping they don't fuck it up.",
